WEBVTT

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:10.980
SWORD GAI

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:27.540
The Shiryu is crying again.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.380
The Shiryu was crying again?

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:41.760
Yes. It seems to be getting louder.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:43.350
I see.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:48.770
I've heard there's another,
inferior version of the Shiryu.

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:51.900
Yeah. Dad told me about it.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:57.320
Maybe this Shiryu is crying
in search of its fellow.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:02.160
Is something so inhuman
as that even possible?

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:03.910
Excuse me.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:07.120
Your expected visitors have arrived.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.170
I see.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:15.210
You want to build an orphanage?

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:20.890
Yes. There's a great building for sale,
formerly an elementary school.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:26.310
It’s abandoned now, but I believe
the location and size are perfect.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:29.350
It's in a beautiful place,
surrounded by nature.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:32.190
I'm sure the children will love it.

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:34.150
Indeed! That's wonderful!

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:38.320
Japan's birthrate is declining,
so children are a valuable resource.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:43.740
And above all, it would make me happy
to help unfortunate children!

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.990
Really?

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.500
Thank you so much!

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.420
I see.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:53.960
You want to build a nursing home
for senior citizens?

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.380
We want to give those
who have bettered Japan

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:02.220
a chance to spend a happy retirement.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:03.550
That's right.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:07.970
There is no greater happiness
than to help lonely elders!

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:09.560
Thank you!

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:14.560
And regarding the building to utilize,
we found the perfect one.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.690
Wonderful!

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:18.690
This is...

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.830
Sayaka, what are you doing?

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:29.330
Father.

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:35.090
Are you thinking about Gai again?

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:39.050
Gai and I have been together
ever since we were kids.

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:41.720
And then he just up and leaves?

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:43.590
Don't you understand?

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:47.890
Gai is guided by
the destiny of the Shiryu.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:53.650
Why did you shape the Shiryu into an arm?
Did you know this would happen?

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:59.230
Gai... What's going to happen to Gai?

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:02.820
Gai is trying to live as a sword.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.320
I simply offered a helping hand.

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:09.330
What's that mean?

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:13.540
Gai's a normal person!
He can't live as a sword!

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:21.720
A sword is fated to kill
from the moment of its birth.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:25.800
But with a sheathe,
it may decide its fate.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:28.680
If Gai is an unsheathed sword,

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:34.560
with humanity as his sheathe,
he may be able to slice open his fate.

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:39.360
Which of these fates will you choose, Gai?

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.490
<i>I know him.</i>

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:50.160
<i>I'm the only one who knows the real Gai.</i>

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:56.460
<i>Hey, Gai, you're still you, right?</i>

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:59.590
<i>The boy who saved me when we were kids.</i>

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.880
<i>That day Gai ran away,
<i>I chased after him.</i></i>

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:07.470
Gai, where are you?

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:09.220
Come out, Gai!

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:13.180
Gai?

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:23.990
Gai!

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:35.540
Oh no! You're bleeding!

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:36.920
I'm fine.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:44.300
Let's go, Gai. Let's go home.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:53.560
<i>Gai came back to protect me that day.</i>

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:57.940
<i>He shed blood for my sake.</i>

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:01.900
<i>I can tell.</i>

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:05.940
<i>Gai is looking up at the same moon I am.</i>

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.830
You're sure you don't want to go
to a hospital?

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:17.210
This is not... oww.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:20.290
Chrysalises heal fast.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:24.210
Well, if you're worried,
try harder to comfort me.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:27.800
I got hurt protecting you, after all.

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:31.640
I didn't ask for that.

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:33.760
You're no fun.

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:36.600
A full moon, huh?

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:40.690
Did you know the light of the full moon
is good for wounds?

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:42.650
Never heard that before.

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:45.280
I bet. It's my personal view.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:47.400
Why did you protect me?

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:50.410
Because you're weak, of course.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:52.530
I'm weak?

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:55.080
Yeah. Incredibly weak.

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:56.910
Are you messing with me?

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:58.750
No, I'm quite serious.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:02.170
Is there a girl you like?

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:04.130
Well?

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:05.590
No.

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:08.380
Sayaka was her name, right?

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:09.300
No.

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:12.840
Is there anyone you want to be with?

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:17.180
I've been alone since I was born.
And I always will be.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.140
That's an easy way to live.

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:23.440
Only a child thinks it's their problem
if they live or die.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:24.940
What are you saying?

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:28.030
You have nothing to protect.
No one to love.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:30.450
Which means you can't protect yourself.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:33.570
Gai, that's why you're weak.

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:42.870
Well?

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:45.000
Perfect for an orphanage, right?

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:48.510
I can just see the happy children!

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.260
Yes, truly.

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:52.550
No, it should be a retirement home.

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:56.350
I think it's the perfect place
to spend a quiet retirement.

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:57.430
Right?

00:07:57.510 --> 00:08:00.520
No, it should be an orphanage!
Orphanage!

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:03.020
It should be a retirement home!
Retirement home!

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:07.650
It's such a nice place, though.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:10.110
Quiet, and with lots of greenery.

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:12.990
-Tokumitsu, my sketchbook.
-Yes, sir.

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:17.830
An orphanage...

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:22.250
A retirement home...

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:28.840
Shinohara! Kurata! I have an idea!

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:30.880
This! Look at this!

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:32.510
This is...

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:36.390
Yes. We can just combine
the retirement home and the orphanage!

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:40.270
The elderly can give the kids
lots of attention,

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:43.020
and it'll be like they have grandkids!

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:45.980
It's two birds with one stone, right?

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:53.070
-Shall we do it then?
-Let's work together.

00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:56.280
Splendidly done, Mr. Shin.

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:59.080
I'm sure your father would be very happy.

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:00.990
I hope so.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:04.500
Both of them are right in their own way.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:07.380
Sometimes combining two opposites
is what opens the way.

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:10.130
That's what I think, Tokumitsu.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:16.260
Is it just me,
or has Sayaka been gloomy lately?

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:18.640
Hey, Sayaka!

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:20.850
Sorry, sorry.

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:23.890
I was just saying
that you've been gloomy lately.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:25.940
That's not true.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:28.020
What is it? Don't hide it.

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:30.940
Let's go somewhere
to get it off your mind.

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:35.240
Let's take the train. I want to try
that cake shop I saw on TV, you know?

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:39.030
I saw that! It's run by a pastry chef
who won a huge award, right?

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:39.990
Sounds great!

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:42.790
You should come with us for once, Sayaka!

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:46.250
Yeah, you're right. Maybe I'll go, too.

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:48.170
Seriously?
You never say that!

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:49.500
Let's do it!

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:56.260
It's been a long time, Kazuma.
Glad to see you're doing well.

00:09:56.630 --> 00:10:00.600
You as well, Mr. Kigetsu.
You look younger each passing year.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.890
What are you talking about?
I already got one foot in the grave.

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:07.560
I came today to discuss Soin.

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:11.610
I have no words to apologize
for the trouble we caused.

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:14.730
Don't worry about it.
The dead are my specialty.

00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:16.900
I gave him a proper burial.

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:22.700
A shame. But to think he failed to notice
the Busoma lurking in his shadow.

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:24.540
We still have much to learn.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:31.460
So, what happened to that Busoma?

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:35.300
I'm not sure.
It disappeared after fighting Gai.

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:36.380
-Gai?
-Yes.

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:39.550
He went with the Shoshidai,
but beyond that...

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:41.050
The Shoshidai.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:43.470
So he's a Chrysalis, then.

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:46.770
An impure being
that will someday become a Busoma.

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:49.350
Don't talk like that.

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:54.190
Both the Shoshidai and you Gabi
wish to defeat the Busoma.

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:56.440
You should work together.

00:10:57.280 --> 00:10:59.150
We do not use weapons.

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:03.740
All we use in battle
are the bodies given to us by God.

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:06.200
We are different from the Shoshidai.

00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:10.960
But not everyone can be like Lady Himiko.

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:15.670
That is why we endure
harsh training every day.

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:19.090
Weapons were made to kill men.

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:22.550
And thus, those who wield them
are damned.

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:26.060
Who knows what Gai
would say hearing that?

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:28.430
This Gai, what is he like?

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:32.400
Someone born with a curse.

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:35.610
His eyes shine like a silver blade.

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:41.400
I love it!

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:44.570
You got some good meat.

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:47.910
It's got the right amount of marbling
for sukiyaki.

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:50.410
There's no chives.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:51.330
Chives?

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:54.250
Yeah. You need chives for sukiyaki.
Go buy some.

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:56.250
Just shut up and eat.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:59.670
If your wounds are healed,
shouldn't we be leaving?

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:02.550
They hurt! They still really hurt!

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:07.260
Is this fun for you?

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:08.810
It sure is.

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:11.980
A lot more fun
than napping at Shoshidai HQ.

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:14.690
If you hate it so much,
why join the Shoshidai?

00:12:14.770 --> 00:12:16.940
Damn, if only I had those chives.

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:18.570
Edible chrysanthemum is better.

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:19.980
-Chives.
-Chrysanthemum.

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:21.990
Wait, it doesn't matter!

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:24.990
I'm asking why you joined the Shoshidai.

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:27.080
You know the answer.

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:28.790
To survive.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:29.950
Survive?

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:31.200
Yeah.

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:33.920
We Chrysalises will someday
become Busoma.

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:38.380
Going into cold sleep
at the Shoshidai can delay that.

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:41.050
Why do you fear becoming a Busoma?

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:46.720
As a Busoma, you cease being yourself.
It's natural to fear it.

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:49.640
You're scared of losing yourself?

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:51.140
I sure am.

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:55.310
I want to stay myself a long time.
Every minute and second that I can.

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:57.110
I don't understand.

00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:59.190
Why cling to yourself?

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:00.980
That's why.

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:04.820
That's why you're weak.
I told you that before, didn't I?

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:07.320
Well, no matter.

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:09.490
It was a long time ago...

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:14.960
Everyone, this way! Hurry!

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:37.770
Damn it.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:40.860
Do you want power?

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:49.780
If you want to survive,
take me in your hand.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:56.370
Kill.

00:13:56.870 --> 00:14:00.000
If you wish to survive, kill everyone.

00:14:00.380 --> 00:14:02.460
-Hey, over there!
-A survivor!

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:03.460
Kill him!

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:35.540
Kei.

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:40.540
Don't let the weapon use you.

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:44.090
Use it for the one you love,
the one you want to protect.

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:46.630
You lack that, so you're weak.

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:49.180
Well, anyway...

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:51.220
Go get some chives!

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:56.020
This is so good!

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:57.060
It's so sweet!

00:14:57.140 --> 00:14:59.940
-I'm so glad we came!
-That one looks good too!

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:01.440
Right, Sayaka?

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:02.980
Oh, yeah.

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:05.980
-Here, try this one too.
-Okay.

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:09.570
That was a nice idea you had, Mr. Shin.

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:12.950
To be expected from
the next head of the Matoba group.

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:15.200
It was nothing that special.

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:17.580
Please sign our petition!

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:19.330
Please sign our petition!

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:21.670
Um, what petition?

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:25.630
That was delicious.

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:27.630
Sayaka, let's come back, okay?

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:30.680
Yeah, I had fun today.
Thank you.

00:15:31.010 --> 00:15:33.680
We're going to hang out a while more.

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:35.260
Yeah, see you later.

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:41.190
What train do I take home?

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:44.440
Um, excuse me! Can you sign this petition?

00:15:44.690 --> 00:15:46.400
-Petition?
-Yes!

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:49.610
Izumi Park, where they intend
to build a condo building,

00:15:49.690 --> 00:15:52.860
has been a very green place,
where locals love to relax.

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:55.830
Is it fine to lose such an oasis?

00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:57.370
No!

00:15:57.620 --> 00:16:01.080
We need to let these foolish politicians
hear our voices!

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:03.000
Please help by signing!

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:04.330
S-Sure.

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:06.340
Thank you!

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:07.960
<i>Now then...</i>

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:08.880
Hey.

00:16:09.090 --> 00:16:10.510
You alone, miss?

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:11.760
Let's hang out!

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:14.470
You're ignoring us?

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:16.350
Th-That's not it.

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:19.930
That's a violation of our rights.
You're under arrest!

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:21.560
P-Please stop.

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:23.060
Come on, just come--

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:23.980
Stop it!

00:16:24.690 --> 00:16:25.610
Who're you?

00:16:26.190 --> 00:16:27.320
She's upset.

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:30.440
If you'll try a crude pick-up...

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:32.610
Then please help by signing!

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:33.820
-Huh?
-What?

00:16:33.910 --> 00:16:36.490
What's his deal? You asshole!

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:39.660
Stop it!
Stop it, please!

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:41.540
Violence?

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:43.710
Why is this happening?

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:46.710
Violence is the dumbest act in the world!

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:50.590
It solves nothing!
It only creates more violence!

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:51.840
Shut up!

00:16:56.890 --> 00:16:57.800
Are you okay?

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:00.560
Um, I'm sorry!

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:04.350
No, don't worry about it.
It's not your fault.

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:07.690
I just can't forgive people like that.

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:12.400
Jeez. What a weirdo.

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:14.240
Don't worry about it.

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:17.450
Forget it, check out that girl!

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:21.580
I like her.

00:17:21.950 --> 00:17:23.330
You alone, miss?

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:25.790
Let's have some fun.

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:27.920
Very well.

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:33.130
She catches on quick.

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:36.090
I guess I'll go... first?

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:44.730
Does it still hurt?

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:48.350
H-Help me! S-Someone--

00:17:53.030 --> 00:17:54.320
Wh-What is...

00:17:55.150 --> 00:17:56.530
What is this?

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:00.780
What was I doing before?

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:04.080
I don't remember at all!

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:05.790
Well, no matter!

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:07.160
Let the game begin!

00:18:11.630 --> 00:18:12.460
G-Gai?

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:20.050
The Shiryu?

00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:29.350
Jeez, where the hell did Gai go shopping?

00:18:35.940 --> 00:18:36.780
Hold on.

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:39.610
Are you... Miura?

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:43.280
Miura was this one's old name.

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:45.410
I am Zsoltgewinn.

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:50.790
I see, so that's how it is.
Didn't think it would be you.

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:54.090
You did a lot for me.

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:57.670
But I'll give you a peaceful rest
by my hands.

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:01.260
You as well... soon enough.

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:04.560
W-Wait!

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:10.980
Damn it!

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:13.900
I can hear the Shiryu's voice.

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:15.400
Who are you?

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:17.070
You're...

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:19.820
I'm the heroine, bitch!

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:26.830
I met you before, right?

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:31.290
Well, it doesn't matter.
Midoriko, the strongest, will kill you!

00:19:38.710 --> 00:19:39.840
The Shiryu.

00:19:56.110 --> 00:19:56.940
Ow...

00:19:57.480 --> 00:19:59.360
He's leveled up!

00:20:12.710 --> 00:20:13.540
Gai?

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:22.630
Oh no! Blood!

00:20:23.260 --> 00:20:24.180
It's nothing.

00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:30.680
Gai, let's go.

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:33.230
Let's go home.

00:20:33.310 --> 00:20:36.610
Stop it. I've got nowhere to go home to.

00:20:36.690 --> 00:20:38.150
-Gai!
-Stay away.

00:20:39.860 --> 00:20:41.360
I'm fine being alone.

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:46.700
Gai.

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:53.290
Everyone, take your seats!

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:58.090
Listen up. I have a new student
to introduce you to.

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:00.840
Everyone, get along with him.

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:08.390
I'm Shin Matoba. Nice to meet you all!
